# Explicit, unambiguous exclusion (the bare ".env" pattern above already
# matches this at any depth, but spelling it out removes all doubt): this
# is the Prisma CLI's test-only env file (see TEST_DATABASE_REPORT.md) and
# must never end up inside a built image. If it somehow did, Prisma's own
# env-loading precedence means an already-set real DATABASE_URL (which the
# container always has, from docker-compose/Render) would still win — but
# there's no reason to ship a test-database connection string in a
# production image at all, so it's excluded outright.
prisma/.env
